      "lineNbr": 682,
      "author": {
        "id": 1960535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-24T04:37:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Is it guaranteed that if \"VendorIdSource\" exists in Floss, then \"SdpDiVendorIdSource\" will also exist for all these instances?\n\nNo, SdpDi* only exists for classic connection. The Vendor* and Product* version exist for both classic and LE.\n\n\u003e For example, will a newly paired classic device in Floss only have the Sdp* versions of these and therefore we miss it in the migration from Floss-\u003eBlueZ?\n\nNo, newly paired classic device in Floss will have both the Sdp* versions and the Vendor* and Product* versions, therefore we will not miss it (that is, unless the user paired the device using pre-M107 floss and migrate to BlueZ after this CL).\n\nLE connections, on the other hand, only have the Vendor* version. Thus, with this CL, we will not miss it on the Floss-\u003eBlueZ migration, whereas it was missed previously.",
      "parentUuid": "bd908013_4ca0198b",
      "revId": "0bd3f19d43cdbe4407d1ab5322e3c6dbb314d1c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
